n    # symlink to root itself\n    os.symlink(root, root / \"self\")\n    expect_reject(root, \"self\")\n    # deeper: self/sub does NOT exist -> resolves to root/sub -> contained -> allowed\n    expect_ok(root, \"self/newthing\", root / \"self/newthing\")\n\n    # symlink pointing inside root -> allowed\n    os.symlink(root / \"a\", root / \"in\")\n    expect_ok(root, \"in\", root / \"in\")\n    expect_ok(root, \"in/b\", root / \"in/b\")\n\n    # relative root\n    cwd = os.getcwd()\n    os.chdir(td)\n    try:\n        expect_ok(Path(\"root\"), \"a/b\", Path(\"root\") / \"a/b\")\n        expect_reject(Path(\"root\"), \"../outside\")\n        os.symlink(\"../outside\", Path(\"root\") / \"relesc\")\n        expect_reject(Path(\"root\"), \"relesc\")\n        expect_reject(Path(\"root\"), \"relesc/new\")\n    finally:\n        os.chdir(cwd)\n\n    # symlink chain out then back in: physically contained -> allowed\n    # root/out2 -> outside_dir2 -> root/a\n    os.symlink(root / \"a\", outside / \"back\")\n    os.symlink(outside / \"back\", root / \"out2\")\n    expect_ok(root, \"out2\", root / \"out2\")\n    expect_ok(root, \"out2/b\", root / \"out2/b\")\n\n    # benign relative-root ..? no—rejected by design\n    print(\"ALL_CHECKS_OK\")\n```\n\nWait — `expect_ok(root, \"self/newthing\")`: joined = root/self/newthing; resolve → root/newthing (since self→root). real_root=root ∈ parents ✓. Returns lexical root/self/newthing. Contained ✓. Good — demonstrates allowed symlink-back-in.\n\nAlso note `expect_reject(root, \"esctd\")` where esctd → td (the parent of root). real_joined = td. real_root = td/root. Is td/root in td.parents? No → reject ✓. And td is an ANCESTOR of root — correctly rejected since we need strict subpath.\n\nHmm wait, one more: `expect_ok(root, \"x\")` where root/x doesn't exist — resolve(root/x) = root/x ✓.\n\nAnd the \"out2/b\" case: root/out2/b where out2→outside/back→root/a. resolve → root/a/b ✓ contained → allowed. \n\nNow, potential issue: `Path.r